  "goodToKnow": "Die Ungleichheit is inequality: soziale Ungleichheit, Einkommensungleichheit, Bildungsungleichheit. Germany's wealth is distributed quite unequally by European standards, even though incomes are more evenly spread. Another topic is the gap between East and West: wages in the former GDR are still lower. Women in Germany earn on average about 18 percent less per hour than men: der Gender Pay Gap. Plural: die Ungleichheiten."
